<header class="ce-hero"><p class="cp-eyebrow">Thoughtfully made. Always improving.</p><h1>A little more room<br>for everyone.</h1><p>We want our apps, tools, and articles to be easy to use. Accessibility is part of how we design, build, and improve them.</p></header>
<div class="ce-prose">
<section><h2>What we are working toward</h2><p>Our target is WCAG 2.2 AA across the site, with enhanced contrast, generous controls, and other AAA improvements where applicable. We have not completed an independent conformance evaluation and do not claim full AA or AAA conformance.</p></section>
<section><h2>Getting around</h2><p>The shared navigation works with a keyboard and without JavaScript. Use Tab to move between links and controls, and Enter or Space to open a menu. With JavaScript enabled, Escape closes a menu and returns focus to its label.</p><p>A “Skip to main content” link appears when you begin tabbing. Our product pages use visible focus indicators, descriptive links, and expandable answers. Your device’s reduced-motion setting is respected by the new navigation and product layouts.</p></section>
<section><h2>Where there is more work to do</h2><p>Interactive tools and games have individual interfaces. Some need JavaScript, and game canvases, live updates, third-party services, and older media need further assistive-technology testing. Contrast and automated checks alone cannot verify that every task is accessible.</p><p>We are continuing to review keyboard operation, screen-reader announcements, zoom, text spacing, media alternatives, and the clarity of our content. Our upcoming podcast will include transcripts.</p></section>
<section><h2>Tell us what gets in your way</h2><p>Please include the page address, what you were trying to do, and your browser or assistive technology if you are comfortable sharing it.</p><a class="cp-button cp-primary" href="mailto:hello@coffeeandfun.com?subject=Website%20accessibility">Email us about accessibility <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p>You can also use our <a href="/support/">support page</a>.</p></section>
<p class="ce-small">Last reviewed: October 1, 2026.</p>
</div>
